OVERVIEW
--------
This KB covers three operational topics for an Inter-Satellite Sync (ISS)
network sync layout:

  1. Trusting self-signed Satellite HTTPS certificates for remote hammer
  2. Listing repositories added on the disconnected Satellite
  3. Synchronizing those repositories (ISS pull from connected to disconnected)

All hammer examples below are intended to be RUN ON THE CONNECTED SATELLITE,
while TARGETING THE DISCONNECTED SATELLITE API with --server.

PLACEHOLDERS
------------

  YOUR_DISCONNECTED_ADMIN_PASSWORD
      Admin password on disconnected Satellite

  sampleorg
      Organization name (use your real org name)

  FQDNs in this document
      Match your DNS / install hostnames


EXAMPLE HOSTNAMES
-----------------

  Connected Satellite:
      connected-satellite.example.com
      Synced from Red Hat CDN; upstream content source for ISS

  Disconnected Satellite:
      disconnected-satellite.example.com
      CDN / content source pointed at connected; pulls via ISS network sync


ARCHITECTURE
------------

  Red Hat CDN
       |
       | sync
       v
  Connected Satellite -------------------- ISS network sync -----------------> Disconnected Satellite
  (has CDN access)                                                              (no direct CDN; uses connected)


  Connected Satellite
      Registers to Red Hat, enables products/repos, syncs content from the CDN.
      Acts as the upstream content source for disconnected.

  Disconnected Satellite
      Manifest imported locally. Content credentials / CDN URL configured to
      the connected Satellite. Enables the same (or subset) of repos and syncs
      from connected over the network (ISS).

  IMPORTANT:
      Enabling a repository on disconnected does NOT download packages by
      itself. You must run a repository/product synchronize on disconnected so
      it pulls content from connected. Connected must already have those repos
      synced from the CDN (or the pull will be empty / fail).


================================================================================
1. SELF-SIGNED CA BUNDLE COMBINATION (FOR REMOTE HAMMER)
================================================================================

Why this is needed
------------------

hammer on connected uses TLS when talking to:

  https://disconnected-satellite.example.com

By default Satellite configures hammer with something like:

  :ssl:
    :ssl_ca_file: '/etc/pki/katello/certs/katello-server-ca.crt'

That file normally contains ONLY the connected Satellite CA. Disconnected has
its OWN self-signed Katello CA. Verification then fails with:

  SSL certificate verification failed
  Make sure the location contains an unexpired and valid CA certificate for
  https://disconnected-satellite...


What "combined bundle" means
----------------------------

A combined CA bundle is a single PEM file that concatenates:

  1. Connected Satellite CA (katello-server-ca.crt from connected)
  2. Disconnected Satellite CA (katello-server-ca.crt published by disconnected)

OpenSSL/hammer can then validate either host certificate chain when using that
file.

NOTE:
  If both Satellites were signed by the SAME custom organizational CA, you
  typically only need that one issuing CA in the trust store, not a per-host
  combine. The steps below assume separate self-signed Katello CAs (common
  default install).


Steps (run as root on CONNECTED Satellite)
------------------------------------------

  DISC=https://disconnected-satellite.example.com
  CA_DIR=/etc/pki/katello/certs
  DISC_CA=${CA_DIR}/disconnected-satellite-ca.crt
  COMBINED=${CA_DIR}/katello-server-ca-combined.crt
  ACTIVE=${CA_DIR}/katello-server-ca.crt

  # 1) Fetch disconnected CA (published over HTTP(S) on /pub)
  curl -k -fsS "${DISC}/pub/katello-server-ca.crt" -o "${DISC_CA}"
  openssl x509 -in "${DISC_CA}" -noout -subject -issuer -dates

  # 2) Backup connected CA
  cp -a "${ACTIVE}" "${ACTIVE}.bak"

  # 3) Build combined PEM (connected CA + disconnected CA)
  cat "${ACTIVE}.bak" "${DISC_CA}" > "${COMBINED}"
  chmod 644 "${COMBINED}" "${DISC_CA}"

  # 4) Install combined as the file hammer already references
  cp -a "${COMBINED}" "${ACTIVE}"

  # 5) Optional but recommended: trust disconnected CA system-wide
  cp -f "${DISC_CA}" /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/disconnected-satellite-ca.crt
  update-ca-trust extract

  # 6) Confirm TLS verify against disconnected
  echo | openssl s_client -connect disconnected-satellite.example.com:443 \
    -servername disconnected-satellite.example.com \
    -CAfile "${COMBINED}" 2>&1 | grep 'Verify return code'
  # Expect: Verify return code: 0 (ok)

Ensure /etc/hammer/cli.modules.d/foreman.yml still has:

  :ssl:
    :ssl_ca_file: '/etc/pki/katello/certs/katello-server-ca.crt'

After step 4 that path IS the combined bundle.


Sanity check
------------

  hammer --server https://disconnected-satellite.example.com \
    -u admin -p 'YOUR_DISCONNECTED_ADMIN_PASSWORD' \
    ping

If SSL is fixed, you should NOT see "SSL certificate verification failed".
Auth errors mean TLS worked but credentials are wrong.


================================================================================
2. REMOTE HAMMER PATTERN (CLI ON CONNECTED -> API ON DISCONNECTED)
================================================================================

Define a reusable prefix on the connected shell:

  export HAMMER_DISC=(
    hammer
    --server https://disconnected-satellite.example.com
    --username admin
    --password 'YOUR_DISCONNECTED_ADMIN_PASSWORD'
  )

  ORG=sampleorg

Examples below use "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" and "$ORG".


================================================================================
3. LIST ALL ADDED REPOSITORIES (ON DISCONNECTED, VIA REMOTE HAMMER)
================================================================================

"Added" repositories are those enabled under the organization (from the
subscription manifest / repository sets).


List repository instances (what will sync)
------------------------------------------

  # Human-readable table
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository list --organization "$ORG"

  # CSV (includes Id - useful for sync-by-id)
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv repository list --organization "$ORG"


List enabled repository sets (what was turned on from the manifest)
-------------------------------------------------------------------

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository-set list \
    --organization "$ORG" \
    --enabled true


List products and how many repos each has
-----------------------------------------

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product list --organization "$ORG"
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv product list --organization "$ORG"


Optional: confirm org name/label
--------------------------------

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" organization list

Use the Title/Name that matches your environment as "$ORG"
(this KB uses sampleorg as a stand-in).


================================================================================
4. SYNC ALL ADDED REPOSITORIES (ISS PULL ON DISCONNECTED)
================================================================================

Connected must already have the same content synced from the CDN. Disconnected
sync jobs pull from the configured upstream (connected).


Option A - Sync by product (recommended)
----------------------------------------

Sync every product that currently has one or more repositories:

  ORG=sampleorg

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv product list --organization "$ORG" \
    | awk -F, 'NR>1 && $5+0 > 0 {print $2}' \
    | while IFS= read -r product; do
        echo "=== Syncing product: ${product} ==="
        "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
          --name "$product" \
          --organization "$ORG" \
          --async
      done

$5 in the CSV is the Repositories count column from:
  hammer --csv product list

Adjust the column index if your hammer CSV headers differ:
  hammer --csv product list --organization "$ORG" | head -1


Option B - Sync every repository by ID
--------------------------------------

  ORG=sampleorg

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv repository list --organization "$ORG" \
    | awk -F, 'NR>1 {print $1}' \
    | while IFS= read -r id; do
        echo "=== Syncing repository id=${id} ==="
        "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository synchronize \
          --id "$id" \
          --organization "$ORG" \
          --async
      done


Explicit product sync examples
------------------------------

  ORG=sampleorg

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
    --name "Red Hat Enterprise Linux for x86_64" \
    --organization "$ORG" \
    --async

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
    --name "Red Hat Satellite" \
    --organization "$ORG" \
    --async

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize \
    --name "Red Hat Satellite Capsule" \
    --organization "$ORG" \
    --async


Monitor sync tasks on disconnected
----------------------------------

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task list --search 'state = running' --organization "$ORG"

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task list \
    --search 'label ~ Actions::Katello::Repository::Sync' \
    --organization "$ORG" | head

  # Follow a specific task:
  # "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task progress --id <TASK_UUID>
  # "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task info --id <TASK_UUID>


After sync - re-check repository state
--------------------------------------

  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository list --organization "$ORG"
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product info \
    --name "Red Hat Enterprise Linux for x86_64" \
    --organization "$ORG"


================================================================================
5. OPERATIONAL CHECKLIST
================================================================================

  1. Connected: repos enabled and synced from Red Hat CDN.
  2. Disconnected: manifest imported; content source / CDN settings point at
     connected.
  3. Disconnected: required repository sets enabled (same labels / releasever /
     basearch as connected where applicable).
  4. Connected: combined CA bundle installed so remote
     hammer --server https://disconnected-... trusts disconnected cert.
  5. From connected: list repos on disconnected -> synchronize products/repos
     on disconnected -> watch tasks until complete.


================================================================================
6. TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

  Symptom: SSL certificate verification failed
    Likely cause: Connected CA bundle missing disconnected CA
    Check: Rebuild combined bundle; confirm ssl_ca_file;
           openssl s_client ... -CAfile

  Symptom: Sync completes but no packages
    Likely cause: Connected never synced that repo from CDN
    Check: On connected: hammer repository list / product sync from CDN

  Symptom: Repo missing on disconnected
    Likely cause: Repository set not enabled
    Check: repository-set list --enabled true; enable matching set

  Symptom: Unable to authenticate
    Likely cause: Wrong user/password for disconnected
    Check: Reset/admin password on disconnected; confirm -u / -p

  Symptom: Sync task fails / timeout
    Likely cause: Network path, firewall, or upstream URL
    Check: From disconnected, HTTPS to connected; firewall/SG port 443;
           CDN URL on disconnected


================================================================================
7. QUICK REFERENCE (COPY/PASTE)
================================================================================

  # --- remote hammer to disconnected ---
  HAMMER_DISC=(hammer --server https://disconnected-satellite.example.com -u admin -p 'YOUR_DISCONNECTED_ADMIN_PASSWORD')
  ORG=sampleorg

  # list
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository list --organization "$ORG"
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" repository-set list --organization "$ORG" --enabled true

  # sync all products that have repos
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" --csv product list --organization "$ORG" \
    | awk -F, 'NR>1 && $5+0 > 0 {print $2}' \
    | while IFS= read -r p; do
        "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" product synchronize --name "$p" --organization "$ORG" --async
      done

  # watch
  "${HAMMER_DISC[@]}" task list --search 'state = running' --organization "$ORG"
